there is growing confusion tonight over  whether president biden feels the  situation along the southern border  is actually a crisis he used that word  saturday for the first time in public  talking about the border but his top  spokeswoman seemed to contradict that  today  white house correspondent kristen fisher  shows us tonight  after weeks of administration officials  describing the situation at the border  as nothing more than challenging  challenges we are  challenged at the border over the  weekend the president himself described  it as a crisis  when explaining why it's taking so long  to raise the refugee cap  the problem was that the refugees were  working on  kevin's up  is that now the official white house  position that there is indeed a crisis  at the border the president does not  feel  that children coming to our border  seeking refuge from violence economic  hardships and other  dire circumstances is a crisis he does  feel  that the crisis in central america the  dire circumstances  that many are fleeing from that he that  that is a situation we need to spend our  time our effort on as the white house  downplays the president's use of the  word crisis  his predecessor is calling it a horrible  situation  there's never been anything like what's  happened at our border  and people are coming in by the tens of  thousands they're walking in they  we had all he had to do is leave it  alone on friday it appeared the white  house was leaving alone the cap on  refugees  that was put in place by the trump  administration only to walk it back  a few hours later after enormous  pushback from democrats on capitol hill  from senator dick durbin to  congresswoman alexandria ocasio-cortez  this has anything to do with the  pushback from democrats  on capitol hill i don't think you've  articulated what our change in policy is  so  go ahead john don't do that well  well you can see the white house press  secretary never really answered  the question there gensake insists this  was all a misunderstanding noting that  the initial order included a caveat  to raise the cap past 15 000 refugees  once that limit  had been reached though gensake also  conceded that the president's  initial promise of raising the refugee  cap to more than  62 thousand now seems unlikely  brett kristen fisher on the north lawn  kristen thanks
 

